#: ../../source/csso_README.md:247
msgid "Usage data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/csso_README.md:249
msgid ""
"`CSSO` can use data about how `CSS` is used in a markup for better "
"compression. File with this data (`JSON`) can be set using `usage` "
"option. Usage data may contain following sections:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/csso_README.md:251
msgid ""
"`blacklist` – a set of black lists (see [Black list filtering](#black-"
"list-filtering))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/csso_README.md:252
msgid "`tags` – white list of tags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/csso_README.md:253
msgid "`ids` – white list of ids"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/csso_README.md:254
msgid "`classes` – white list of classes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/csso_README.md:255
msgid ""
"`scopes` – groups of classes which never used with classes from other "
"groups on the same element"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/csso_README.md:257
msgid ""
"All sections are optional. Value of `tags`, `ids` and `classes` should be"
" an array of a string, value of `scopes` should be an array of arrays of "
"strings. Other values are ignoring."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/csso_README.md:259
msgid "White list filtering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/csso_README.md:261
msgid ""
"`tags`, `ids` and `classes` are using on clean stage to filter selectors "
"that contain something not in the lists. Selectors are filtering only by "
"those kind of simple selector which white list is specified. For example,"
" if only `tags` list is specified then type selectors are checking, and "
"if all type selectors in selector present in list or selector has no any "
"type selector it isn't filter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/csso_README.md:263
msgid "`ids` and `classes` are case sensitive, `tags` – is not."
msgstr ""

